LadrunoSANISAND nDMaterial - Ladruno subclass of ManzariDafalias (model: A.Ghofrani, P.Arduino, U.Washington); settable p_residual/p_min. ADR 86.
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: p_residual = 0 (default, cohesionless), pRe = 1 (user, ELASTIC-ONLY floor: G, K ~ sqrt(max(p + pRe, p_min)/P_atm); yield surface, psi, M^b, M^d, D and p_min UNCHANGED -- ADR 93 II.1), p_min = 0.101 (user), honorTolR = 0 (ModifiedEuler substep TolE = 0.0001, vanilla's hardcoded value), TanType = 2 (consistent mCep_Consistent (unsymmetric)), maxSubsteps = 20000 (ModifiedEuler FAILS the update past this many substeps, so the step can be cut), reversalTol 1e-10 (undoes integrate()'s mAlpha_in loading-reversal reset when ||eps - eps_n|| falls below this, i.e. treats it as round-off noise), reversalRel 0.05 (SECOND threshold = reversalRel * ||last committed d_eps||; a hold's noise tracks the solver tolerance, not round-off, so the absolute test alone under-catches it); reversal test skipped on dt == 0 (ops_Dt, unconditionally -- a hold has no loading to test for a reversal in); hold-skip commits counted in implexGuards[5] [D5b: D_factor sigmoid non-dimensionalised in vanilla (PR-2), an exact no-op at P_atm = 101; D5a: whether it should exist at all once the residual pressure is zero is still OPEN]
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: -flipAlphaIn vanilla (flip: alpha_in := alpha (vanilla, the DEFAULT: unchanged -- the base's own loading-reversal sign test decides, which Esmeralda measured is deterministic and correct on a real deck once the reversal-noise guard is confined to primed states -- see P2-7c)), -implexFlipAbsorb OFF (the DEFAULT: the flip commits nothing beyond mElastFlag's own effect on the next real step -- required for the ADR-92 gate-5 -implex ON-vs-OFF byte-identity on a zero-free-DOF deck)
